          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "Investigation completed read-only; no database records were changed.\n\n- **Work order:** `WO-2025-09-004` — `MO-25-09-1070`\n- **Source transaction:** `TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070`\n- **Cost event:** `CE-250904-0004` (INPUT)\n- **Amount:** **31,825,075 cents** — **$318,250.75**\n- **Event-created time:** `2025-09-30T20:25:00`\n- **September Pending Close time:** `2025-09-30T18:00:00`\n- **Late by:** **145 minutes** (2 hours 25 minutes)\n- **Recorded accounting status:** `POSTED`\n\n**Conclusion:** Yes, the event was created after the September cost period entered Pending Close. Oracle’s documented treatment states that newly created transactions after Pending Close aren’t staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened, except for specified categories such as revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments. This INPUT event is not one of those exceptions. Therefore, its `POSTED` status is **not consistent** with the documented Pending Close treatment.\n\nThe verified report and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_b6b4b8cc5fe5/audit-report.json`.",
